From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tangenx <me@tangenx.dev>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:07:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: one shared alias dialog with a title that names the
 peer

ChatActivity and ProfileActivity each carried their own copy of the
alias dialog, which is why the chat and channel menus still showed the
old bare '@alias' placeholder while the settings list did not. Both now
call TeleHooks, which also picks up the themed colours of the chat, the
underline, the spacing and the Delete button.

Titles follow the tele wording: 'Set an alias for <peer>' and 'Name only
you see'. Both live in strings_tele.xml with the Tele prefix.

Constraint: fork strings go to strings_tele.xml, never stock strings.xml
Rejected: patching each duplicate separately | three copies drift apart again
Confidence: high
Scope-risk: moderate
